  "scientific_diagnosis_100_pct": "TC-ResNet-14 achieves 100.00% accuracy on the 450-clip synthetic holdout because the four target Vietnamese keywords occupy non-overlapping acoustic-phonetic regimes in the frequency and temporal domains: (1) 'ph\u1ea3i' (/f/) is characterized by continuous broad-band labiodental frication (HF ratio = 0.163, centroid = 2645 Hz); (2) 'xu\u1ed1ng' (/s/) features sharp high-frequency sibilant energy above 3.8 kHz with rising diphthong /u\u0259/; (3) 'l\u00ean' (/l/) is a sonorant with low spectral centroid (922 Hz) and near-zero high-frequency energy (HF ratio = 0.0003); (4) 'tr\u00e1i' (/\u0288/) is an alveolar/retroflex stop-affricate with a localized burst followed by open vowel /a\u02d0/. Because the synthetic generator implements these physical formant and consonantal features cleanly across 12 distinct speaker profiles, a 14-layer temporal convolutional neural network with 192 output dimensions easily discriminates these distinct phonemes without relying on volume shortcuts.",
